Dear collegues,

I am very new in the world of imperfect detection modeling, but I am really amazed by what someone can do with this powerful tool.

I am now trying to apply the unmarked package to deal with imperfect detection in my dataset. I have 56 sites in which I made 2-3 replicates. I used the pcount function because I believe that's my case and then I manged to correct several different taxa for imperfect detection.

However, some of then presented really low values of detection, so for those I got stuck in the problem of finding the appropriate boundary. Moreover, if i try to use the ranef function to see the corrected abundances I recieve many NaN (not a number) outcomes.
I see this as an ongoing challenge in the development of more appropriate equations to handle those low values, but I am also would like to question the necessity of correcting something which does seem to be well detected.

Then because of my problem I also have a doubt: If the detection bias is low does it mean it is ok to not consider a imperfect detection? Is it ok for those well detected taxa if I just use the mean + 95%CI for estimate the abundance in the site?

