Sounds like potentially an issue described in this thread (and paper referenced within): https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/unmarked/_WO5U7AeYdQ ...in which case, yeah, it may not make sense to present the N-mixture abundance estimates. Perhaps a different mixture distribution provides more reasonable results (see again the referenced the Dennis et al. 2015 paper, and the AHM book Ch. 6 [I think] has a more in depth discussion; also, some of the earlier chapters in the book may provide some useful background, such as the effect of un-modeled heterogeneity on parameter estimation)?

Best,

John

